      "text": "**Short answer:** A good beginner agentic AI project is small, uses one or two real tools, has a clear goal and a stop condition, and shows that you can **test** what the agent does. Start with a single tool-using agent (projects 1-4 below), add retrieval and memory (5-7), then try orchestration, MCP and multi-agent designs (8-10). For each project, publish the code, a README with an architecture diagram, a small evaluation set and a short note on what went wrong and how you fixed it. That is what turns a demo into a resume project."
